e court is considering bail. Both Daniel and Beth remained silent during police questioning. Which of the following statements is correct?", "A": "The DPP must instruct the jury to draw ‘unfavourable inference’ for Beth.", "B": "The judge may allow the jury to draw ‘unfavourable inference’ for Beth but not Daniel.", "C": "The judge must allow the jury to draw ‘unfavourable inference’ for Daniel.", "D": "The judge must allow the jury to draw ‘unfavourable inference’ for Beth and Daniel.", "Code": "C119", "Answer": "B"}, {"Syllabus point": "Nature of crime", "Question": "Which of the following elements of homicide distinguishes murder from manslaughter?", "A": "Actus reus", "B": "Mens rea", "C": "Causation", "D": "Consent", "Code": "C12", "Answer": "B"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Investigation Process", "Question": "Raynor has been detained by police because it is suspected that he will commit a terrorist act next week. Which of the following statement is correct?", "A": "Raynor does not have the right to contact a lawyer", "B": "Raynor is being held in protective custody", "C": "Raynor is being held in continued detention", "D": "Raynor has the right not to be questioned by police during his detention", "Code": "C120", "Answer": "D"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Investigation Process", "Question": "Which of the following is true in relation to the right to silence, in NSW, for a person over 18?", "A": "It exists in all circumstances.", "B": "Summary offences are exempt.", "C": "Courts may later draw an unfavourable inference.", "D": "It is a right at the police station but not during court proceedings.", "Code": "C121", "Answer": "C"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Investigation Process", "Question": "Francis is 15 years old and has been arrested for a motor vehicle theft. Which of the following statements is correct?", "A": "Bail must be granted because Francis is aged under 18.", "B": "Bail could possibly be granted to Francis by the bail authority.", "C": "Bail