istrate to increase the limits.", "D": "May ignore these limits in extreme circumstances.", "Code": "C127", "Answer": "A"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Investigation Process", "Question": "In some Australian states, legislation that will allow police officers to issue on-the-spot fines to offenders who possess small quantities of illicit drugs has been proposed. The purpose of this legislation is to", "A": "Avoid the use of courts", "B": "Promote recidivism", "C": "Promote restorative justice", "D": "Enforce the use of custodial sentences", "Code": "C128", "Answer": "A"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Investigation Process", "Question": "While on her way to work, Samantha was stopped by police for a random drug test. After the drug test the police wanted to search the car. Are they permitted to do so?", "A": "Yes, but only if they have reasonable grounds to suspect that Samantha is in possession of a prohibited drug", "B": "No, it is an illegal search", "C": "Yes, the police are always allowed to search a motor car", "D": "No, the police must always have a search warrant", "Code": "C129", "Answer": "A"}, {"Syllabus point": "Nature of crime", "Question": "After an argument, Asha stabs Melissa with a kitchen knife. Melissa has a medically diagnosed weak heart and consequently suffers a heart attack and dies. Asha is charged with Melissa’s murder. What element of crime will be most difficult to establish in this case?", "A": "Strict liability", "B": "Actus reus", "C": "Mens rea", "D": "Causation", "Code": "C13", "Answer": "D"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Investigation Process", "Question": "In which of the following investigation processes is a search warrant required?", "A": "To record phone conversations", "B": "To question a suspect", "C": "To stop a person driving a stolen car", "D": "To search a car suspected of being involved in a break and enter", "Code": "C130", "Answer": "A"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Investigation Process", "Question": "In which of the 