ch is offered a charge negotiation in return for information about other participants in the crime. Which of the following best explains the charge negotiation process?", "A": "All charges will be dropped and Zach will be released", "B": "Zach will plead not guilty and will be allowed to go free", "C": "Zach will plead guilty and the jury will pass sentence", "D": "Zach will plead guilty and the judge will likely pass a lesser sentence in return.", "Code": "C146", "Answer": "D"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Trial Process", "Question": "Why is the availability of Legal Aid important in the criminal justice system?", "A": "It assists the judge in a sentencing decision.", "B": "It allows the accused to represent themselves.", "C": "It supports the accused to seek legal representation.", "D": "It ensures that both sides have access to legal resources.", "Code": "C147", "Answer": "C"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Trial Process", "Question": "How is the right to legal representation best described?", "A": "It is a right limited under common law.", "B": "It is a right protected under the Australian Constitution.", "C": "It is a right to free legal aid provided in most criminal cases.", "D": "It is a right protected under the Universal Declaration of Human Rights.", "Code": "C148", "Answer": "A"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Trial Process", "Question": "Of the following, the person most likely to be granted legal aid under NSW law is a person:", "A": "Who pleads guilty", "B": "Involved in a divorce", "C": "Accused of a serious crime", "D": "Appealing a criminal conviction.", "Code": "C149", "Answer": "C"}, {"Syllabus point": "Nature of crime", "Question": "Which of the following statements is true of causation?", "A": "It is relevant to all criminal offences.", "B": "It is relevant to those offences which include some element of harm or end result.", "C": "If there is a novus actus interveniens, the accused will found guilty.", "D": "The accused’s actions must be the sole cause of the victim’s harm.", "Code": "C15", "Answer": "B"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Trial Process", "Question": "When assessing an application for legal aid for a person accused of a crime, what does the means test refer to?", "A": "The nature of the crime", "B": "The assets and income of the applicant", "C": "The likelihood of a not guilty verdict in the trial", "D": "Whether the accused meant to commit the crime", "Code": "C150", "Answer": "B"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Trial Process", "Question": "What are the requirements for the granting of legal aid?", "A": "Admit to your crime", "B": "Pass the jurisdiction test only", "C": "Pass the merit and means test", "D": "Pass the merit, means and jurisdiction test", "Code": "C151", "Answer": "D"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Trial Process", "Question": "Kevin is granted legal aid for his murder trial in the Supreme Court. However, legal aid is denied for the appeal against his conviction. What is the likely reason for this?", "A": "He failed the means test.", "B": "His case did not satisfy the merit requirements.", "C": "His case did not meet the jurisdictional requirements.", "D": "Indictable offences do not meet legal aid requirements.", "Code": "C152", "Answer": "B"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Trial Process", "Question": "The right to legal representation in NSW is characterised by which of the following statements?", "A": "It does not exist at all.", "B": "It is guaranteed for all NSW residents.", "C": "It is a limited common law right.", "D": "It is a statutory right for all criminal offenders.", "Code": "C153", "Answer": "C"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Trial Process", "Question": "Mary aged 16 has been charged with murder. The evidence suggests she was the Principal in the 1st degree. Mary has told her lawyer that she was acting under duress. Her lawyer gives her the following information: Duress can be used as a defence for murder, and she may qualify for legal aid. Why is some of this informa