y harm to John", "Code": "C158", "Answer": "C"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Trial Process", "Question": "Which of the following encroaches upon the right criminal standard of proof of ‘beyond reasonable doubt’?", "A": "Unanimous verdicts", "B": "Majority verdicts", "C": "Bail", "D": "Parole", "Code": "C159", "Answer": "B"}, {"Syllabus point": "Nature of crime", "Question": "A teenager picks up a backpack when leaving a party. When they arrive home, they find that while the backpack is identical to their own, it belongs to someone else. What element of crime did the teenager NOT exhibit?", "A": "Mens rea", "B": "Causation", "C": "Actus reus", "D": "Doli incapax", "Code": "C16", "Answer": "A"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Trial Process", "Question": "The standard of proof for criminal offences is higher than for civil offences. This is because:", "A": "Criminal trials take longer than civil trials", "B": "Criminal matters are more complex than civil matters", "C": "Criminal matters involve more significant consequences for the accused", "D": "Juries may not understand what ‘on the balance of probabilities’ means", "Code": "C160", "Answer": "C"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Trial Process", "Question": "Evidence is seized during a police search of a property. Which of the following statements is true?", "A": "The evidence is admissible if the police had a warrant.", "B": "Police do not have the power to seize evidence from properties.", "C": "The evidence is admissible if it is in the public interest to seize it.", "D": "The evidence is only admissible if the suspect is present during the search.", "Code": "C161", "Answer": "A"}, {"Syllabus point": "Criminal Trial Process", "Question": "Which of the following statements is TRUE regarding the rules of evidence?", "A": "Generally, evidence cannot be given about the bad character of the accused", "B": "Witnesses may give their opinion about another person’s words, appearance or actions", "C": "Witnesses are allowed to 