n offender to serve six months in gaol, to be served only if the offender is not of good behaviour during this time. This is an example of:", "A": "Probation", "B": "Imprisonment", "C": "A suspended sentence", "D": "A diversionary program", "Code": "C235", "Answer": "C"}, {"Syllabus point": "Sentencing and Punishment", "Question": "Mark is charged with an offence and the matter is brought to court by a police prosecutor. It is his first offence. Mark is found guilty and sentenced. What type of offence would most likely apply to Mark?", "A": "A summary offence and a fine", "B": "A summary offence and imprisonment", "C": "An indictable offence and a suspended sentence", "D": "An indictable offence and a good behaviour bond", "Code": "C236", "Answer": "A"}, {"Syllabus point": "Sentencing and Punishment", "Question": "A person who has no previous criminal record commits a minor crime. The judge finds the person guilty of the offence but does not record a conviction. What is this an example of?", "A": "Judicial error", "B": "Restorative justice", "C": "Judicial discretion", "D": "A suspended sentence", "Code": "C237", "Answer": "C"}, {"Syllabus point": "Sentencing and Punishment", "Question": "What is the purpose of diversionary programs?", "A": "To involve the victim in sentencing", "B": "To prevent future criminal behaviour", "C": "To deter crime by increasing penalties", "D": "To remove potential offenders from society", "Code": "C238", "Answer": "B"}, {"Syllabus point": "Sentencing and Punishment", "Question": "A man is convicted of using offensive language in a public place and the magistrate imposes a punishment of 3 penalty units. This means the man", "A": "Must pay a sum of money", "B": "Receives 3 demerit points", "C": "Must serve 3 days in prison", "D": "Receives a variety of punishment", "Code": "C239", "Answer": "A"}, {"Syllabus point": "Nature of crime", "Question": "Ben helps Di to plan a bank robbery. Di attempts to commit the bank robbery but is unsuccessful. Which of the following statements is correct?", "A": "Ben has committed a preliminary crime; Di has committed a white-collar crime", "B": "Ben is an accessory before the fact; Di is an accessory after the fact", "C": "Ben and DI have both committed preliminary crimes", "D": "Ben and Di are both principals in the first degree", "Code": "C24", "Answer": "C"}, {"Syllabus point": "Sentencing and Punishment", "Question": "New legislation proposes mandatory sentencing. A judge comments that the proposed legislation challenges judicial discretion. The judge is able to make these comments based on which legal principle?", "A": "Precedent", "B": "Ratio decidendi", "C": "Division of powers", "D": "Separation of powers", "Code": "C240", "Answer": "D"}, {"Syllabus point": "Sentencing and Punishment", "Question": "While serving a custodial sentence, a murderer writes a book about her crime. She is not permitted to keep the money from the book sales. This means that the court has made an order for", "A": "Continued detention", "B": "The payment of a fine", "C": "The forfeiture of assets", "D": "Participation in a rehabilitation program", "Code": "C241", "Answer": "C"}, {"Syllabus point": "Sentencing and Punishment", "Question": "Which of the following is a feature of a NSW Criminal Infringement Notice (CIN)?", "A": "It is issued by a court.", "B": "It cannot be overturned in court.", "C": "It is an alternative to court prosecution.", "D": "It is always followed by a court proceeding.", "Code": "C242", "Answer": "C"}, {"Syllabus point": "Sentencing and Punishment", "Question": "John, who is 17 years old, is charged with grievous bodily harm. He has a number of prior convictions for violent assault. What penalty is John most likely to receive?", "A": "Control order", "B": "Suspended sentence", "C": "Home detention order", "D": "Community service order", "Code": "C243", "Answer": "A"}, {"Syllabus point": "Sentencing and Punishment", "Question": "Which of the following is true o