ing is to", "A": "Reduce recidivism.", "B": "Investigate crimes.", "C": "Reduce rehabilitation.", "D": "Impose mandatory sentences.", "Code": "C264", "Answer": "A"}, {"Syllabus point": "Sentencing and Punishment", "Question": "Fred is charged and found guilty of drug trafficking. The judge reviews the statutory guidelines before handing down the sentence. Which of the following does NOT reflect the statutory guidelines?", "A": "Maximum sentencing", "B": "Mandatory sentencing", "C": "Standard non-parole period", "D": "The application of precedent", "Code": "C265", "Answer": "D"}, {"Syllabus point": "Sentencing and Punishment", "Question": "A major attack on a religious building in Sydney CBD has taken place causing serious damage. Several similar attacks have also taken place recently. The judge is persuaded by the prosecution who have reinforced the severity and frequency of the crime taking place in the community. The judge decides upon a lengthy custodial sentence. Which factors are impacted upon sentencing?", "A": "Objective features, including deterrence", "B": "Subjective features, including remorse", "C": "Objective features, including prior convictions", "D": "Subjective features, including limited emotional harm", "Code": "C266", "Answer": "A"}, {"Syllabus point": "Sentencing and Punishment", "Question": "A high-risk offender is detained further at the end of their sentence term. Which of the following best describes this?", "A": "Procedural fairness", "B": "Continued detention", "C": "Community Correction Orders", "D": "Denial of the presumption of innocence", "Code": "C267", "Answer": "B"}, {"Syllabus point": "Sentencing and Punishment", "Question": "Ezra, who is 19 years of age, pleads guilty to manslaughter 2 weeks before his trial in the District Court is due to commence. Which of the following statements is correct?", "A": "Ezra may receive a suspended sentence.", "B": "Ezra will not be eligible for a sentencing discount.", "C": "Ezra may be eligible t